---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout>
  <header id="intro" class="page">
    <h1>My journey with three.js journey</h1>
    <p>
      Welcome to this website where I'll share various exercises and experiments
      done while learning Three.js from the&nbsp;<a
        href="https://threejs-journey.com/"
        target="_blank">Bruno Simon's three.js journey lessons</a
      >.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <h2 class="bookmark"><a href="#chapter1">Chapter 1 : Basics</a></h2>

    <div id="chapter1" class="page">
      <p>
        This first chapter is all about fundamentals : geometries, materials,
        textures... Everything needed to create my first Three.js scenes.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="/threejs-journey-projects/chapter1/hello-world"
            >Hello world !</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page:first-child {
    z-index: 0;
  }

  .page:target {
    z-index: 1;
  }

  ul {
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    list-style-type: none;
  }

  .bookmark {
    position: absolute;
    left: max(15rem, 66vw);
  }

  section:nth-of-type(2) .bookmark {
    top: 2em;
  }

  section:nth-of-type(3) .bookmark {
    top: 4em;
  }
</style>
